      "explanation": "Reordering the loops to i\u2011k\u2011j improves cache locality. The original i\u2011j\u2011k order accesses b column\u2011wise (stride n) causing many cache misses. By iterating k outermost, we load each a[i][k] once and then stream through the k\u2011th row of b (contiguous) while updating the entire row of c, reducing memory traffic and speeding up the matrix multiplication without changing any observable behavior.",
